# What the build context must NOT carry.
#
# `.env` FIRST, and it is load-bearing rather than tidy: it is the only file in
# the repository that holds a credential (the Copernicus Marine login, and the
# Bhashini key once it exists). A `COPY . .` anywhere, now or in a future edit,
# would bake it into an image layer that outlives every later change to it.
.env
.env.*

# Rebuilt inside the image, or not needed in it at all.
**/node_modules
**/.next
.venv
**/__pycache__
**/.pytest_cache
apps/web/public/cesium

# Large, gitignored, and mounted at runtime rather than baked in.
data

# Local artefacts.
test-results
playwright-report
docs/evidence
docs/submission
.ppt-build
.git
.remember
